# The Linux kernel compilers' patch series (aarch64, x86_64, powerpc), applied
# in this order by scripts/build-linux.sh to stock GCC 16.2.0 and binutils 2.47.
# One line per patch: the source tree it goes into (gcc or binutils), then its
# path under patches/. Lines starting with "#" are notes.
#
# Only fixes that are not AmigaOS's: fold-mem-offsets (0019) is a fix in GCC's
# target-independent pass, so it goes in. The AmigaOS driver, libnix,
# pthreads (aros-stuff) and libstdc++ patches stay out; the identity
# (GFOpenAmigaGCC 16.2.0-openN) is given by --with-pkgversion, as for m68k-aros.
# tests/linux-recipe.sh checks every patch here is one the stock-GCC m68k-aros
# series applies too, and that it is no m68k or AmigaOS patch.
gcc       gcc/0019-fold-mem-offsets-a-memory-to-memory-move-is-no-root.patch
